  "summary": "SFPD disabled NCRIC and Western States Information Network access to its Flock ALPR network after a routine audit found 299 improper queries by out-of-state and federal agencies over roughly a year. Police said no ICE or DHS queries were involved and no immigration or reproductive-rights inquiries were found.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "There were 299 improper inquiries over approximately one year, which account for 0.005% of inquiries over that period",
      "paragraph_idx": 14
    },
    {
      "quote": "Upon discovering the improper searches, Chief Derrick Lew immediately turned off NCRIC's access to SFPD's ALPR system and initiated an internal review",
      "paragraph_idx": 16
    },
    {
      "quote": "California law places clear restrictions on sharing license plate reader information with out-of-state or federal agencies.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    }
  ],
